# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_4033093> (limbal epithelial stem cell of cornea)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20614614") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29105366") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36983561") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37768272") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_4033093> "A stem cell that is part of the corneo-scleral limbus. This cell type resides at the basal layer of the epithelium and has a small size and high nuclear to cytoplasmatic ratio (Secker and Daniels, 2009). A limbal stem cell is responsible for corneal epithelial renewal and repair (Li et al., 2023), and to help maintain a clear corneal surface by preventing conjunctival epithelial cells from migrating onto the cornea (Wang et al., 2023).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20614614") <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_4033093> "limbal epithelial stem cell")
